WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:05.980
<i>Mash's life in a magic school to become
a Divine Visionary has begun.</i>

00:06.650 --> 00:08.570
<i>Although he can't use magic.</i>

00:09.230 --> 00:11.610
<i>Although he can't use magic!</i>

00:12.990 --> 00:16.990
Finn, can you lend me
a broom for tomorrow's class?

00:17.530 --> 00:20.740
I actually brought a burdock,
thinking it was a broom.

00:20.830 --> 00:23.790
Burdock? You thought
a burdock was a broom?

00:23.790 --> 00:24.750
Accidentally.

00:25.000 --> 00:26.790
Accidentally?

00:27.590 --> 00:29.500
Okay. I'll lend you one.

00:29.880 --> 00:32.460
I knew you were a great guy.

02:04.970 --> 02:08.730
Today, you will learn how to ride a broom.

02:08.940 --> 02:12.820
Channel magic energy into the broom
and command it with the word "fly."

02:12.820 --> 02:16.360
Then straddle it and regulate the magic
to keep it afloat.

02:16.530 --> 02:18.240
Now, begin.

02:18.490 --> 02:21.990
- Fly.
- Fly!

02:23.870 --> 02:29.250
Pops. I'll become number one
and restore our peaceful life.

02:30.710 --> 02:31.670
Okay.

02:33.340 --> 02:34.300
Fly.

02:36.460 --> 02:37.380
Fly.

02:38.170 --> 02:39.090
Fly.

02:39.840 --> 02:40.760
Fl...

02:43.140 --> 02:44.180
Fair enough.

02:44.180 --> 02:48.060
Come on now,
you can't even get a broom to float?

02:48.310 --> 02:51.650
Looks like one of us needs the remedial class.

02:51.850 --> 02:56.070
You're slowing the rest of us down.

03:00.530 --> 03:01.660
Fly.

03:04.660 --> 03:07.160
Th-That's cheating, you worm.

03:07.910 --> 03:11.710
Quit acting innocent.
It flew up before you commanded it.

03:13.130 --> 03:14.250
Why you...

03:14.250 --> 03:17.760
Now, how fast can your broom go?

03:17.760 --> 03:20.050
We will now begin the timed trials.

03:20.800 --> 03:24.260
Perfect timing. How about a little race?

03:24.260 --> 03:30.560
Loser has to obey the winner
for as long as we're here. Up for it?

03:30.680 --> 03:31.560
Sure.

03:35.650 --> 03:36.730
<i>Idiot.</i>

03:36.730 --> 03:41.950
<i>Unlike transfers, I've been riding brooms
since middle school.</i>

03:42.240 --> 03:44.700
<i>There's no way I'd lose
to someone like you.</i>

03:45.030 --> 03:47.240
<i>Prepare to get swept.</i>

03:48.490 --> 03:52.410
<i>That student...
It's the class clown from yesterday.</i>

03:53.120 --> 03:55.250
<i>Can he even ride a broom?</i>

03:55.420 --> 03:57.090
All right, on your marks.

03:57.460 --> 03:59.340
Ready... go.

04:02.880 --> 04:04.010
<i>What the...</i>

04:04.680 --> 04:06.890
<i>What the heck did I just witness?</i>

04:07.390 --> 04:08.470
No!

04:08.470 --> 04:13.100
What incredible speed! A new world record
has been set! A world record!

04:13.480 --> 04:15.060
What just happened?

04:15.060 --> 04:16.360
Didja see that?

04:16.360 --> 04:17.610
I have no clue.

04:20.480 --> 04:22.610
<i>I got a good look.</i>

04:23.280 --> 04:25.780
<i>As soon as she said "start,"
he chucked the broom.</i>

04:25.990 --> 04:28.830
<i>Then he immediately
jumped out towards the broom.</i>

04:29.160 --> 04:33.210
<i>He used air resistance to decrease
his speed, closed the gap to it,</i>

04:33.540 --> 04:34.960
<i>and mounted it in midair.</i>

04:36.330 --> 04:37.710
<i>How is that even possible?</i>

04:38.090 --> 04:41.210
You must have cheated.
There's no way that happened!

04:41.840 --> 04:45.590
Can't face the facts, huh?
I feel kinda bad for you.

04:45.590 --> 04:46.760
Why you...

04:46.760 --> 04:50.560
It's okay. I'll drop the bet, too.
I feel sorry for you.

04:51.350 --> 04:52.770
You mocking m...

04:55.230 --> 04:57.860
Hey, now. Let's not make a scene.

04:58.020 --> 05:00.730
Sorry. My apologies for his rudeness.

05:01.030 --> 05:03.490
This guy here is my friend.

05:03.690 --> 05:05.740
Huh. Well, okay.

05:06.240 --> 05:08.780
Uh-oh. Cavill's talking to him?

05:08.780 --> 05:10.620
He's totally the target now.

05:10.620 --> 05:12.240
We'd better stay out of it.

05:12.240 --> 05:14.500
He's the first victim in high school.

05:14.710 --> 05:18.380
Anyway, what you did earlier
really caught my attention.

05:18.380 --> 05:20.420
Would you like to be friends with me?

05:20.710 --> 05:21.630
Huh.

05:21.840 --> 05:24.670
I'm Lloyd Cavill. Nice to meet you.

05:27.720 --> 05:29.390
Spud Cabbage?

05:35.980 --> 05:39.860
Excuse me, what are you all doing?
We're in the middle of class.

05:39.860 --> 05:41.400
Oh, whoops.

05:42.230 --> 05:46.900
You're pretty funny. You should
come here again after school.

05:47.570 --> 05:48.910
I'll be waiting.

05:50.490 --> 05:51.620
Huh.

05:53.160 --> 05:54.700
Middle of class...

05:55.660 --> 05:59.170
As for you... Why'd you have to go
and lose like that?

05:59.170 --> 06:01.170
That was pretty pathetic, you know?

06:01.590 --> 06:04.340
You got made fun of instead.

06:06.170 --> 06:08.840
What a loser you are.

06:09.260 --> 06:12.300
You just couldn't follow simple orders.

06:13.010 --> 06:16.520
I simply told you
to go mess with him.

06:19.150 --> 06:20.690
Oh, well.

06:21.190 --> 06:24.440
At least I found a good toy.

06:25.820 --> 06:27.440
Who was that guy?

06:27.780 --> 06:31.370
Cavill is a continuing student
from the middle school division, like me.

06:31.490 --> 06:34.950
So why is everyone afraid of him?

06:36.370 --> 06:37.870
That's because...

06:40.330 --> 06:44.500
Because he's the son of a high-ranking member
at the Bureau of Magic.

06:45.170 --> 06:49.970
Even you must know that the Bureau of Magic
is absolute in this realm.

06:50.300 --> 06:53.220
O-Of course, I know that.

06:54.560 --> 07:00.310
Well, simply put, if you
stand against him, you get expelled.

07:01.310 --> 07:04.270
The vice principal seems to have
close ties with his family.

07:04.270 --> 07:07.690
Get on their bad side,
and they'll force you to drop out.

07:08.240 --> 07:13.120
As a continuing student, I saw it happen
too many times since middle school.

07:13.370 --> 07:17.290
For some, the torment
doesn't end after dropping out either.

07:17.870 --> 07:21.000
That's why everyone obeys him.

07:21.420 --> 07:22.920
They're scared.

07:25.710 --> 07:27.510
<i>It's after school.</i>

07:31.630 --> 07:34.390
It's fun to make some
on your own every so often.

07:38.180 --> 07:42.140
I wish Pops could taste
these cream puffs, too.

07:42.770 --> 07:44.980
<i>Well, the choice is yours.</i>

07:44.980 --> 07:47.480
<i>Spend the rest of your life
being hunted down,</i>

07:47.480 --> 07:50.860
<i>or brace yourself to die
and try turning the tables.</i>

07:51.900 --> 07:55.740
I have to become the top student
in this academy no matter what.

07:58.700 --> 08:00.620
I feel like I'm forgetting something.

08:02.040 --> 08:03.210
Oh, well.

08:03.210 --> 08:06.920
<i>Mash ticked off someone
who you really shouldn't cross.</i>

08:08.420 --> 08:10.130
<i>The next day.</i>

08:10.670 --> 08:13.380
The next class is Potions, so...

08:16.470 --> 08:17.640
Oh no.

08:18.220 --> 08:20.430
My textbook is falling apart.

08:26.440 --> 08:28.020
Hello.

08:29.190 --> 08:32.150
You didn't show up yesterday.
What were you doing?

08:33.570 --> 08:35.780
Oh, I'm sorry.

08:35.780 --> 08:37.410
I was making some cream puffs.

08:41.120 --> 08:45.580
Anyway, I heard you're aiming
to be the Divine Visionary.

08:45.580 --> 08:49.420
I'm good friends with the vice principal,
so I have some connections.

08:49.630 --> 08:54.930
If you do what I tell you, I could put in
a good word for you. What do you say?

08:55.180 --> 08:57.760
Really? Whoopee. I'll do it.

08:58.510 --> 09:00.060
But why so suddenly?

09:00.060 --> 09:04.270
Well, you seem like a fun person,
and I want to help out.

09:04.270 --> 09:07.020
But it'd be weird to have
no strings attached, right?

09:07.020 --> 09:07.940
Good point.

09:08.900 --> 09:12.820
So, for starters, carry these for us.

09:12.820 --> 09:13.440
'Kay.

09:13.740 --> 09:16.160
Ugh, my shoes are dirty. Wipe them for me.

09:16.160 --> 09:16.950
'Kay.

09:17.160 --> 09:19.030
- Gimme a drink.
- 'Kay.

09:19.030 --> 09:20.910
- Massage my shoulders.
- 'Kay.

09:20.910 --> 09:23.620
- Do something funny.
- ‘Kay.

09:23.830 --> 09:25.960
'Kay.

09:26.750 --> 09:29.710
Next class is, let's see...

09:32.050 --> 09:34.010
Another textbook torn up.

09:34.970 --> 09:37.220
Finn, can you show me your textbook?

09:38.930 --> 09:42.720
S-Sorry. Ask someone else to...

09:44.180 --> 09:44.980
Thanks.

09:45.480 --> 09:47.600
Um, I said no...

09:48.900 --> 09:50.610
You're a real lifesaver.

09:51.190 --> 09:53.690
And thanks for the broom yesterday.

09:53.940 --> 09:55.740
These cream puffs are my thanks.

09:55.740 --> 09:57.450
Uh, okay.

09:59.700 --> 10:01.700
But I really am glad.

10:03.330 --> 10:06.250
To have a great guy like you for a friend.

10:10.380 --> 10:11.460
Yeah.

10:11.960 --> 10:14.420
Wow, you're such a great guy.

10:14.420 --> 10:16.970
I'm totally in your debt. You're a lifesaver.

10:17.760 --> 10:21.720
Don't even mention it.
You've been a big help.

10:29.600 --> 10:33.440
Sorry, sorry. I spilled some.
Clean it up, will you?

10:34.360 --> 10:36.440
Hm? What's wrong?

10:36.900 --> 10:38.740
You will do it, won't you?

10:40.070 --> 10:42.950
So Potions is up next.

10:43.580 --> 10:46.330
I really don't like that teacher.

10:46.330 --> 10:48.830
Maybe I'll have
the vice principal have them fired.

10:49.000 --> 10:51.500
Ain't that a little extreme?

10:55.130 --> 10:57.720
It's so clean it sparkles.

11:01.800 --> 11:02.720
Oh.

11:03.470 --> 11:06.140
I can't believe he does whatever we say.

11:06.140 --> 11:08.140
Maybe he'll catch on soon?

11:08.140 --> 11:10.390
I'm getting bored of textbooks.

11:10.390 --> 11:12.730
Next, I want you to burn his clothes.

11:13.110 --> 11:14.900
Got that, Finn?

11:15.730 --> 11:19.150
If you go that far,
maybe he'll quit school on his own?

11:19.360 --> 11:21.240
I can't do this anymore.

11:21.360 --> 11:25.740
What was that?
I didn't quite hear you. Say it again.

11:27.160 --> 11:28.250
I said...

11:28.450 --> 11:31.000
I can't do this anymore.

11:34.670 --> 11:36.420
I see.

11:40.590 --> 11:42.800
You've made a mistake.

11:42.800 --> 11:45.640
When you make a mistake,
you drop down and beg for forgiveness.

11:49.480 --> 11:51.890
Where did Finn go?

11:52.690 --> 11:55.190
I accidentally
took his textbook with me.

11:57.820 --> 11:59.280
What's that sound?

12:08.370 --> 12:10.410
M-Mash.

12:11.580 --> 12:13.500
If it isn't Mash.

12:15.130 --> 12:16.420
What are you doing?

12:17.500 --> 12:19.670
Getting an apology.

12:19.920 --> 12:22.470
Because he got a bit ahead of himself.

12:26.600 --> 12:28.510
Are you okay, Finn?

12:29.010 --> 12:29.970
Yeah.

12:30.270 --> 12:31.430
But you're bleeding.

12:32.430 --> 12:35.520
That doesn't matter right now, Mash.

12:38.770 --> 12:41.820
I-It was me.

12:42.320 --> 12:47.070
The one who ruined your textbooks...
It was me.

12:47.780 --> 12:49.080
I was ordered to.

12:49.080 --> 12:51.540
I was too scared to disobey.

12:51.540 --> 12:55.080
But you kept saying I was a great guy.

12:55.290 --> 12:58.000
You called me your friend, but...

12:58.000 --> 13:02.050
Still, I did horrible things to you.

13:02.050 --> 13:05.220
So I just... I needed to apologize to you.

13:05.890 --> 13:09.680
I'm so very sorry. Sorry.

13:10.010 --> 13:14.270
If only you'd honestly
apologized to me like that...

13:14.560 --> 13:19.320
Oh, by the way, I'm about
to dine with the vice principal.

13:19.320 --> 13:21.110
Care to join us, Mash?

13:21.320 --> 13:24.240
You can leave that dirty little lackey here.

13:24.650 --> 13:27.620
I've been dying to introduce you.

13:28.070 --> 13:31.240
You might never get a chance like this again.

13:31.540 --> 13:35.000
Especially if you keep company
with someone who only apologizes, like him.

13:41.340 --> 13:44.090
You're the one who should apologize.

13:50.010 --> 13:52.180
You're the one who should apologize.

13:53.470 --> 13:54.270
Wut?

13:54.480 --> 13:57.020
Double wut?

13:58.150 --> 14:01.190
Th-That'll get you expelled.

14:04.110 --> 14:06.280
Is that a big deal?

14:07.280 --> 14:08.780
Mash.

14:10.450 --> 14:11.280
Oh.

14:12.490 --> 14:13.790
Maybe it is a big deal.

14:17.540 --> 14:19.540
I might've done something bad.

14:19.710 --> 14:22.800
Yes, that's right.
You have done something bad.

14:23.300 --> 14:26.050
V-Vice Principal Farman.

14:28.550 --> 14:30.430
What are you doing here?

14:30.430 --> 14:35.060
This young boy's father
entrusted me with his son.

14:35.560 --> 14:38.310
I witnessed the entire incident.

14:38.770 --> 14:40.150
If you witnessed the whole thing, then—

14:40.150 --> 14:42.820
This was a violent attack on a student.

14:43.070 --> 14:45.860
Finn Ames and Mash Burnedead.

14:45.860 --> 14:49.070
We will hold a school conference
regarding your roles in this incident.

14:49.070 --> 14:49.950
Huh?

14:50.490 --> 14:53.080
Surely you can see why
if you think about it.

14:53.080 --> 14:56.830
You two and he are of different status.

14:57.160 --> 14:59.920
Different social status
means different treatment.

14:59.920 --> 15:02.670
Are you too ignorant
to figure that out, you idiot?

15:02.670 --> 15:05.750
Then, I will enlighten you idiots.

15:05.750 --> 15:09.840
This is how the world operates.

15:10.130 --> 15:11.800
<i>The vice principal.</i>

15:11.800 --> 15:13.850
<i>Not him too.</i>

15:16.270 --> 15:19.600
He didn't seem that open to reason,
so I couldn't help it.

15:20.310 --> 15:22.520
But really, after one, what's one more?

15:22.520 --> 15:24.360
<i>That's serial killer logic!</i>

15:25.650 --> 15:27.690
You assaulted me.

15:27.690 --> 15:33.620
I can expel ordinary students
like you at any time.

15:33.910 --> 15:35.240
Lepios Oga.

15:38.950 --> 15:40.620
What is this?

15:40.920 --> 15:43.380
Dirt?

15:43.750 --> 15:44.630
Wha...

15:48.050 --> 15:49.880
What... Sto...

15:50.090 --> 15:52.130
What do you think you're doing?

15:54.010 --> 15:55.140
Burying you.

15:55.350 --> 15:58.560
And you think you can get away with this?

15:58.560 --> 16:00.180
- I can have you—
- Just like...

16:00.940 --> 16:03.690
you can expel me at any time,

16:04.690 --> 16:07.270
I can bury you at any time.

16:07.980 --> 16:14.160
Throw me in prison. Or cut my body in two.
Even if I have to crawl over, I will bury you.

16:16.160 --> 16:18.910
Wait... Stop... Cut it out!

16:19.120 --> 16:21.910
I'm serious! Stop!

16:22.000 --> 16:26.670
Stop it. No!

16:29.420 --> 16:33.930
I assume you know why
you were summoned here?

16:34.390 --> 16:37.390
Because I made cream puffs
in the dorm kitchen without asking.

16:37.390 --> 16:38.930
Completely wrong.

16:41.770 --> 16:46.190
You punched young Cavill,
and buried the vice principal.

16:46.400 --> 16:50.440
This issue was seen as a problem
over at the Bureau of Magic.

16:51.360 --> 16:57.450
Here. I have a notice from the Bureau of Magic
to expel you immediately.

16:57.740 --> 17:01.370
The Bureau of Magic
is this country's highest legal authority.

17:01.370 --> 17:04.500
It's no stretch to say they control this country.

17:04.620 --> 17:08.380
At the core of their organization
are the Divine Visionaries.

17:08.540 --> 17:14.300
This academy furnishes the Bureau
with those qualified to become Divine Visionaries.

17:14.720 --> 17:20.470
As I'm sure you're aware, young Cavill
is a high-ranking member's son of the Bureau.

17:21.020 --> 17:22.640
In other words...

17:22.850 --> 17:25.900
You have done something unforgivable.

17:32.360 --> 17:33.740
However...

17:34.900 --> 17:40.490
What is even more unforgivable is a world
where the caring are at a disadvantage.

17:41.120 --> 17:45.500
I've been concerned
by the current state of things in this world.

17:45.830 --> 17:49.460
Which is why I took
this position several years ago.

17:49.460 --> 17:55.420
Currently the world turns with authority,
power, and the self-serving at its center.

17:55.420 --> 18:00.680
We have frighteningly few people like you,
who sacrifice themselves and act.

18:01.260 --> 18:05.890
The Divine Visionaries who lead
the Bureau of Magic have a role.

18:05.890 --> 18:09.520
That role is to carefully consider
what the people desire.

18:09.900 --> 18:17.570
That is why I sincerely hope that someday,
someone like you will become a Divine Visionary.

18:17.570 --> 18:20.160
No need to tell me. I already plan to.

18:21.950 --> 18:24.160
Wonderful. That's the spirit.

18:24.450 --> 18:28.250
Allow me to explain how you will do that.

18:28.370 --> 18:29.420
'Kay.

18:29.670 --> 18:34.670
To be chosen as a Divine Visionary,
you must be the top student at this academy.

18:34.670 --> 18:39.930
That requires gathering enough coins
through schoolwork and activities.

18:40.260 --> 18:43.640
There are three types of coins.
Gold, silver, and bronze.

18:43.640 --> 18:47.180
The type of coin you receive
is further differentiated by task.

18:47.390 --> 18:52.940
It is tradition that every year, those who have
a certain number of gold coins... Huh?

18:53.650 --> 18:55.690
He's passed out.

18:56.110 --> 18:59.360
I overloaded him with information
to the point of unconsciousness.

18:59.910 --> 19:02.830
Mash. Mash!

19:03.780 --> 19:06.950
I'm sorry. I was overloaded with information,
so I couldn't help it.

19:07.750 --> 19:11.460
Sorry. Let me condense it for you.

19:11.710 --> 19:18.220
Earn high marks in your classes and school activities.
And acquire as many coins as possible.

19:18.670 --> 19:22.970
I will handle the vice principal
and the Bureau of Magic.

19:23.260 --> 19:24.970
Do you understand, Mash?

19:25.060 --> 19:27.140
I am counting on you.

19:27.470 --> 19:28.730
'Kay.

19:29.020 --> 19:30.810
Then I'll be going now.

19:33.560 --> 19:39.900
<i>There is one more problem
you will eventually have to face.</i>

19:40.820 --> 19:43.490
<i>But I have faith in you.</i>

19:43.570 --> 19:46.160
<i>That you can overcome it.</i>

19:48.330 --> 19:51.120
<i>And thus, Mash ended up
with no punishment.</i>

19:51.580 --> 19:54.750
<i>However, by defeating
the infamous Cavill and vice principal,</i>

19:55.130 --> 19:59.220
<i>he became someone who was acknowledged
by the other students.</i>

20:00.470 --> 20:04.550
When making cream puffs, it's all about
preventing the batter from cooling.

20:04.550 --> 20:06.760
Uh, wow, I see.

20:06.760 --> 20:08.520
You there, with the mushroom head!

20:08.850 --> 20:12.440
How would you like to represent
Adler dorm in a Duelo match?

20:12.440 --> 20:15.810
And let's burn out together
in this fire that we call life!

20:19.280 --> 20:22.400
It's Lord Tom,
last year's Duelo MVP of the year.

20:22.400 --> 20:25.910
He's such a sportsman that his stuffiness
actually works well for him.

20:25.910 --> 20:29.540
And what's with that guy with that hairdo?
Totally a fungus.

20:29.540 --> 20:31.540
Bet he collects pill bugs at home.

20:33.040 --> 20:35.460
So, what is Duelo?

20:35.540 --> 20:37.550
And what's this fire that we call life?

20:37.710 --> 20:39.920
We compete using our brooms.

20:39.920 --> 20:42.220
It's the number one sport in the Magic Realm.

20:42.220 --> 20:45.890
A first-year playing Duelo? That's amazing.

20:45.890 --> 20:47.680
But I can't ride a broom.

20:48.890 --> 20:52.270
Don't be modest.
You blew everyone away in class.

20:52.270 --> 20:54.690
Why are you shouting? Also, I said...

20:55.770 --> 20:58.690
The game's tomorrow.
We're counting on you.

20:59.570 --> 21:00.230
But I...

21:00.570 --> 21:03.400
Shoot for the stars. Even if you miss,
you'll land among your dreams.

21:03.400 --> 21:05.950
This guy's denser than I am.

21:10.660 --> 21:12.120
Hey, I'm counting on you.

21:12.120 --> 21:14.120
I heard you got a new world record?

21:14.120 --> 21:16.080
Today's game is gonna be a piece of cake.

21:16.080 --> 21:17.330
Let's give it our all.

21:18.090 --> 21:20.460
But I can't ride brooms.

21:23.050 --> 21:27.760
<i>The first Duelo match this season
is Adler dorm vs. Lang dorm.</i>

21:27.760 --> 21:33.520
<i>Which team will win this match
and earn silver coins?</i>

21:35.480 --> 21:36.690
Go for it!

21:38.020 --> 21:39.150
What's with him?

21:39.150 --> 21:41.150
It's like he's not even trying to fly.

21:42.230 --> 21:46.240
Well, I said I can't ride brooms, so...

21:46.990 --> 21:49.330
If you don't wanna be here, then go home!

21:49.330 --> 21:51.990
- Stop screwing around!
- Go home already!

21:53.200 --> 21:54.500
I want to go home.

21:54.500 --> 21:57.000
<i>If you go home, you won't be able
to become a Divine Visionary.</i>

21:57.670 --> 22:02.840
<i>In order to regain your peaceful life
with Pops, fly. You have to fly, Mash.</i>
